<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Limbaži</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lemsal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Limbaži, German Lemsal, is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidzeme">Vidzeme</a> region of northern Latvia, north-east of Riga. It grew up around a castle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a>, later archbishops, of Riga on lands once held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonians">Livonians</a>, and became one of the oldest towns in the country and a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a>. It is now the centre of Limbaži Municipality.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/limbazi.jpg" alt="Limbaži" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Laima Gūtmane (simka) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Limba%C5%BEu_vecpils%C4%93ta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
